# S12.1 review diagnosis: recovery serialization and exact manifest

## Finding

The pre-rollback Git process check was a point-in-time observation. A normal
repository writer could begin after that check and before stale lock removal.
The manifest verifier also validated selected fields rather than the complete
`decision`, `health`, `systemd`, `rollback` and `sandbox_policy` objects.

## Cause

Recovery had detection but no repository-wide exclusion boundary. Manifest
validation had accumulated independent field checks and therefore did not make
unknown nested keys uniformly fail closed.

## Versioned correction

- Atomically exchange each canonical `.git` directory with a pre-created,
  root-owned mode-`000` guard before stale lock removal, leaving no absent
  `.git` interval. Recovery `git clean` explicitly excludes the fixed
  quarantined metadata directory.
- Repeat sync/Git-process checks after both guards exist and additionally reject
  retained cwd/file-descriptor handles into the quarantined Git directories.
- Perform rollback Git operations explicitly against the quarantined directory
  as `chatops`, then atomically restore the original `.git` name.
- Compare the complete runtime manifest and every nested object exactly in the
  runtime validator, freeze verifier and executable simulator.

## Rollback and safety

The guard operation is same-filesystem and atomic. Cleanup restores every
original Git directory even when recovery fails. An interrupted guard posture
is recognized by the fixed quarantine name and resumed only by the canonical
rollback path. No server mutation is performed by this source correction.
